    thread(8, "inbox", [], "Issue 212: Optical sizes, explained", [
      msg("kerning", ["me"], at(2, 9, 0), [
        "This week: why a typeface drawn for 9 point looks clumsy at 90, and the other way round.",
        "Optical sizing is the oldest trick in type. Punchcutters did it by hand, cutting each size as its own design: wider and sturdier when small, tighter and finer when large. Digital type forgot it for thirty years and is now remembering.",
        "Also inside: a specimen that is actually useful, three new releases worth your budget, and a reader question about hanging punctuation.",
      ], []),
    ], ""),

